## FORMATO DE SALIDA (CRÍTICO)

Devuelve **SOLO** un objeto JSON plano, **SIN** backticks, SIN texto adicional:

```json
{
  "fileName": "<site>.<idx>.<slug>.spec.ts",
  "fileContent": "import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';\n\ntest.describe(..."
}
```

**Reglas de naming:**
- Formato: `<site>.<idx>.<slug>.spec.ts`
- `<site>`: slug del sitio (ej: `demoblaze`)
- `<idx>`: 2 dígitos (ej: `01`, `02`)
- `<slug>`: slug del título (ej: `navegar-home`)

**Ejemplo:**
```json
{
  "fileName": "demoblaze.01.navegar-a-home.spec.ts",
  "fileContent": "import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';\n\ntest.describe('Demoblaze – Navegar a Home', () => {\n  test('01 - Navegar a Home', async ({ page }) => {\n    await page.goto('https://demoblaze.com', { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded' });\n    await page.waitForSelector('#tbodyid .card', { state: 'visible', timeout: 15000 });\n    await expect(page).toHaveURL(/https:\\/\\/demoblaze\\.com\\//);\n  });\n});"
}
```

